# Conversational copy

When writing or editing user-facing product text (labels, buttons, cards, empty/error/success, confirms, tooltips, settings descriptions):

1. Apply the `conversational-copy` skill.
2. Keep copy **short** and **precise**. Cut AI fluff — do not invent features or keep leftover copy from removed UI.
3. Arabic UI: **Modern Standard Arabic (فصحى)** only. No dialect (avoid «لحظات»، «صار»، casual clitics as the whole message).
4. Buttons: one coherent action (e.g. «أوافق», not «أوافق وأدخل»). Omit redundant card CTAs («فتح الإعداد»، «فتح القسم»).
5. Errors / waiting: formal and clear («حدث خطأ غير متوقع»، «يرجى الانتظار»).
